{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1520668-unified-origin-for-sorcerers","id":1520668,"title":"Unified origin for sorcerers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-15T07:22:01-07:00","id":1520668,"title":"Unified origin for sorcerers?","content":"Is there any official content that gives a unified origin for sorcerers, like how Kindred come from Caine and Garou come from Gaia and Luna and mages are humans who have Awakened the power to manipulate Quintessence? I read the M20 Sorcerer and I couldn\u2019t find anything like this. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T07:35:32-07:00","id":1520669,"title":"","content":"The most common theory I've seen is that sorcerers are mortals that make use of Mythic Threads to produce supernatural results.<br /> <br /> In general, it's best to keep in mind that sorcerers <i>aren't</i> Awakened or Embraced, nor do they undergo anything like a Chrysalis or a First Change: they're mortals who only differ from the average mortal in that they have a mindset that's conducive to working sorcery \u2014 represented in M20 Sorcerer by them having a Focus. And even that's not necessarily all that essential, as Vampire, Werewolf, and (indirectly) Wraith all have mortals who practice Hedge Magic, and none of <i>them</i> (explicitly) have a Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-15-2023, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T07:35:45-07:00","id":1520670,"title":"","content":"I think Sorcerers were never given a concrete origin, they were just assumed to be part and parcel of the World of Darkness from the get-go. People tend to forget that Sorcerers didn't originate in Mage: The Ascension but in the first edition of Vampire: The Masquerade, which contrary to what some V5 fans and devs will tell you, was the most urban fantasy and &quot;D&amp;D-like&quot; of all the editions of the VTM line. <br /> <br /> The earliest rules for playable Sorcerers were found in The Hunters Hunted. In that book, Hedge Magic was still just called Thaumaturgy, and it was implied that the Magi of WoD at the time were a lot closer to Sorcerers than Awakened. The other scant anf fleeting appearances of Magi in VTM 1e also implied that as well.<br /> <br /> At some point in early 1993, during the development of Mage, the decision to create the Awakened and separate Hedge Magic from the spheres of True Magick occurred and the term &quot;Sorcerer&quot; was coined to describe those hedge magic-using wizards from VTM 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:13:05-07:00","id":1520674,"title":"","content":"The publication history of Hedge Magic:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Hunters Hunted</b> introduced Thaumaturgy for mortal hunters, and was presented as a \u201clesser version\u201d of the vampiric Discipline of the same name.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Ascension's Right Hand</b> debuted Hedge Magic for the first time. All subsequent \u201cmortal sorcery\u201d systems have been based on this. Its explanation for Hedge Magic is that it involves harnessing the power of a Sleeping Avatar.<br /> <br /> 3. The various <b>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</b><i>Year of the Hunter</i> supplements introduced new Paths for Hedge Magic: <b>The Inquisition</b> provided four Paths of Theurgy (Via Medicamenti, Via Ignis, Via Geniorum, and Via Necromantiae); <b>Project Twilight</b> added Divination; <b>Halls of the Arcanum</b> added Alchemy; and <b>The Quick and the Dead</b> added Cursing, Fetishism, Ephemera, and Spirit Control.<br /> <br /> 4. This was followed up by the release of <b>Sorcerer: the Hedge Wizard's Handbook</b>, which collected and standardized the Paths published to date, as well as adding some new ones. It also attempted to provide a unified explanation for sorcerers, as it now called all practitioners of Hedge Magic; but that explanation was even more vague than the one provided in <b>Ascension's Right Hand</b>.<br /> <br /> 5. After <b>Mage Revised</b> came out, there was an editorial mandate to do a <b>Sorcerer Revised</b>. This book introduced terminology such as \u201cLinear Magic\u201d; and rather than explaining the phenomenon of sorcery, it pushed the idea that, in practice, the mage and the sorcerer really aren't all that different.<br /> <br /> 6. The release of the 20th Anniversary gamelines brought about a new wave of books featuring Hedge Magic: <b>Hunters Hunted II</b>, <b>Kinfolk: a Breed Apart</b>, and <b>Ghost Hunters</b> (which technically isn't a <b>Wraith</b> supplement, but actually is).<br /> <br /> 7. Finally, <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> is based on a (far superior, IMHO) <i>Storyteller's Vault</i> product called <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b>, which introduced the concept of Focus to sorcery and otherwise served mainly to update <b>Sorcerer Revised</b> to <b>M20</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-01-2024, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:18:48-07:00","id":1520676,"title":"","content":"WOD Sorcery is a learned ability to use ones will and tap into forces that are, like physical forces, simply part of the universe. A Sorcerer's paradigm might inform how they explain those forces, but none of them is either right or wrong - the Sorcerers themselves are part of the equation that makes Sorcery work, so whatever rationale someone is using concerning the source of the power just has to work for the individual. But: These forces may also be powerful entities.<br /> <br /> Tracing the roots of Sorcery in WOD canon is pretty difficult because there isn't much in terms of direct history, just conjecture from info on sorcerous groups, their interaction with other splats, and so on. I filled in the patchwork with some head-canon and what I know about magic in RL history to answer 'where does it come from' for myself like this:<br /> <br /> - The first instances were likely <i>invocation magic</i>. Calling on an outside source for power, like Spirits, gods, demons, etc. This is less active magic because you either channel the power of another being or directly ask an entity to intervene on your behalf. Mechanically, this was separated into True Faith and certain Numina that allow for communication with other entities. The ceremonial magic for this is called <i>Rite</i>.<br /> <br /> - This later developed into a more formalized application where the source of power became diffuse and dependent on Paradigm, with the caster themselves changing from conduit to component. Instead of invocations you have <i>spells</i>, and the ceremonial version is called <i>Ritual</i>.<br /> <br /> All these variants still exist in parallel today, and some of them are actively petitioning outside powers - Shamanism for example. The confusing part starts when some powers clearly exist in the WOD (Spirits, Ghosts, Demons), while others are ambiguous (deities). The generally agnostic outlook of most WOD material tends to place the power center at the caster, regardless of Paradigm, even when this results in conflicts with how the powers are described to work. Side note, this is less ambiguous for Psychic Phenomena, where the 'magic' is squarely an ability of the caster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:30:51-07:00","id":1520679,"title":"","content":"I keep saying Paradigm, but the correct term is Focus for Sorcerers, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> said. Probably because I disagree with how WW used those terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T08:43:14-07:00","id":1520682,"title":"","content":"You have tradition on your side: M20 changed things up, renaming what previous editions had called \u201cParadigm\u201d as \u201cFocus\u201d, \u201cPhilosophy\u201d or \u201cTheory\u201d as \u201cParadigm\u201d, and \u201cFocus\u201d as \u201cInstrument\u201d. And it formalized the terminology, as previous editions only formally defined foci. <br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer M20's terminology; but to each their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T17:04:25-07:00","id":1520722,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys. And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> I agree with your last post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-17T18:09:15-07:00","id":1520850,"title":"","content":"NWoD's Second-Sight hints at belief for hedge-magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.